Ensign Peters jumped out of the car and escaped.

00:51:08.020 --> 00:51:09.960
Vons, a drugstore just off G Street.

00:51:11.020 --> 00:51:12.260
Vons, off G Street.

00:51:12.490 --> 00:51:12.810
Right.

00:51:32.840 --> 00:51:33.280
Thank you.

00:52:24.800 --> 00:52:25.400
They're looking for us.

00:52:26.700 --> 00:52:27.560
First, the chicken or the...

00:52:30.000 --> 00:52:31.040
Williams is here, sir.

00:52:31.400 --> 00:52:32.040
Send him in.

00:52:41.780 --> 00:52:42.340
Bad time.

00:52:43.030 --> 00:52:43.550
Yes, sir.

00:53:00.060 --> 00:53:05.790
been part of a war game, the most vital one this country has ever had. War game?

00:53:05.970 --> 00:53:12.260
The test are atomic defenses. You hit on the answer before we were ready. You mean

00:53:12.260 --> 00:53:16.540
Commander Jackson and Ensign McGrew were the enemy? That's right. Commander

00:53:16.540 --> 00:53:20.230
Jackson is our expert on atomic demolition and you discovered I was the

00:53:20.230 --> 00:53:24.340
one who ordered the metal cases. Did you know this all the time? Hadn't the

00:53:24.340 --> 00:53:28.160
slightest idea until you cabled for permission to arrest Jackson and McGrew

00:53:28.160 --> 00:53:29.820
then we were informed.

00:53:30.090 --> 00:53:35.520
the war game. Then why did you keep me captive on the sub? Couldn't give it away until the

00:53:35.520 --> 00:53:40.200
game was over and we knew how we stood. For a while there, it looked as though we had no

00:53:40.200 --> 00:53:47.670
defense against the real thing. But it's finished now, Johnny, and you did a great job. That

00:53:47.670 --> 00:53:52.140
torn sleeve, we weren't staked out for you. I was slipping the last of the uranium aboard

00:53:52.140 --> 00:53:57.450
the sub when I ran into you and Andre on a dock. Couldn't take a chance. For a game,

00:53:57.450 --> 00:53:59.980
you play pretty rough. Sneaking atom bombs it.

00:54:00.000 --> 00:54:05.200
the country's a rough business. Look at that hot rod kid Jonesy. War games accidents happen.

00:54:06.530 --> 00:54:11.120
And the whole thing was make-believe. Even the suspects we picked up. Most of them military

00:54:11.120 --> 00:54:17.380
personnel trained for the job and let loose. Forty-eight of them to be exact. Forty-eight.

00:54:19.080 --> 00:54:28.390
Forty-eight bags. One for each state. Kind of symbolic, huh? Forty-eight man wasn't picked up till an hour ago.

